# Companion locomotion — do not mix Surface / Galaxy 2D with XR follow

**User-locked 2026-08-24.** Evidence: both panel-2D clients log `mode {immersive:false}` + `2d locked`.

## Contract

| Context | Behavior |
|---------|----------|
| **Surface PC embed** | Locked — no camera follow, no 0.5 m distance rule, no `walk.vrma` |
| **Galaxy XR 2D panel** (not Enter VR/MR) | Same lock |
| **Galaxy Enter VR / Enter MR** | World **anchor** on entry → **follow** only after headset moves ≥ 0.5 m (1 m standoff + depart/arrive + `walk.vrma`) |

## Forbidden regressions

- `followEnabled = immersive \|\| !embed` (made Surface chase the camera)
- Continuous follow the moment immersive starts (kills world anchor)
- Default `allowDistanceWalk = true` on `OrcustAutomaton` (must default **false**)
- Relying on nulling `currentTarget` alone while Arrive stays active

## Source of truth

- Policy: `chat/app/src/lib/companion-locomotion-policy.ts` (+ tests)
- Runtime: `galatea.tsx` — `lockPanel2d()` before **and** after `entityManager.update`, plus world XZ pin
- Package: `allowDistanceWalk` / IdleState / WalkState gates

## After `chat/app/src/` edits

`bash OpenNexus3DStudio/scripts/sync-companion-to-surface.sh` — hard-refresh existing OpenNexus 3D tab (no new browser tab).
